y their  collective bargaining agreement is a  living document adding as we move  forward in time and our industry adapts  to changes there will be a need to make  modifications Omaha Nebraska  like San Antonio allows officers to  review video evidence before they're  interrogated access to the video is only  there to help refresh the officers  memory so their officer is given the  most accurate statement to the incident  in Nebraska officer misconduct records  are confidential  Anthony Connor is president of the Omaha  Police Officers Association is it  possible for people in Omaha to see the  disciplinary records of police officers  similar to other public sector employees  no it's not do you think it should be to  gain the public's trust actually no I  don't want to try to situation but  whether it's George Floyd or the  incident Alanna you hear the argument  that the person's history doesn't matter  well if the history don't matter with  them why would it matter what a police  sauce yes that's where I think there's  some confusion and what the public says  they want well I guess the difference  would be one person is being paid to  protect people and the other is just a  citizen presumed innocent I can  recognize that but at the same time I  still think that personnel records  should not be open but kana does support  president Trump's recent executive order  calling for a database to track officers  excessive use of force you should not  have police officers that are fired from  one agency for misconduct and then hire  Galman down the road how does it feel to  hear the criticisms of unions in this  larger discussion of implementing  reforms it's kicking us out of the room  and not having us as part of the  conversation does the public have any  input in these police union contracts  yes they do because the public votes for  the mayor who's actually going to sign  the contract they vote for a city  council who votes for the contract where  a police department doesn't have the  resources to meet the financial demands  of the police unions an easy way to  settle that negotiation is to make some  concessions on discipline it's easy to  just blame the union but that doesn't  really get at the problem these  contracts didn't write themselves so the  question that is why are our political  leaders signing off on these bad deals  all across the country as negotiations  continue during Cole's for police reform  hole  local officials accountable Russian says  is essential the CBS this morning  Errol Barnett New York sounds like he's  right there this all comes down to  politics  alright Errol thank you very much
 

